WEBVTT

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.790
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:17.080
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.640
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.890
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.490
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:40.800
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.080
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.210
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:52.080
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:56.060
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.830
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:04.260
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.770
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.000
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:15.200
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.800
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.040
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.420
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.460
03rd Team, moving out!

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.750
Hey! Hey!

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.290
You fill your stomach,
you're back in the fight!

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.520
Shut up!

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.430
We can't pull outta here
until the 08th Team gets back!

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.200
Dammit! Hey, where's
Lieutenant Nickard?

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:50.070
Looks like he's still
on lunch break...

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.930
You dumbshit! Are you
trying to kill us?!

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.050
That looks about done.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.580
Sorry we're late!
Can we get resupplied?

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.690
Take what you need
by your own damn SELF!

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.760
Hey, that looks
really tasty!

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.900
Looks like your
commander's pretty late.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.970
Never mind that.
Can we have some of that?

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.630
No way.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.670
You stingy old mule!

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.010
Insults don't help you.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.370
Oh, yeah. I think some
mail came for you guys.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.730
Go and get it, Michel.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.620
Huh? But that stew's
got bacon in it!

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.150
I said go get it!

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.520
All right, all right...

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:43.650
You bring that mail here
as fast as you can!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.990
Right.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:45.980
Christ!

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.700
What's with that shit-eating
grin on your face?

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.700
Well, the truth is, this is
a little gift from my goddess.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.290
Your GODDESS?

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:59.310
A lady named Maria who lives...

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:01.430
...in the village by the lake
to the west of here.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.670
How many decades ago was she
a "goddess," you horny old fart?

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:08.730
Eledore!

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.510
You got a letter!

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.440
For me?

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.210
There you go.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.470
Is it bad news?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.410
Eledore...

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.300
I've done it!
I've finally done it!

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.570
What is it?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:40.880
Hold on to your hat! My song's
getting a major debut!

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.780
They're gonna press my song!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.740
I guess I should say
congratulations.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.450
Hell yes, you should!
Throw me a damned party!

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.050
That's right!
Let's have a party!

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.830
Who knows when the commander
and the others will get back.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:55.760
Let's go!

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.640
To where?

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.860
Just leave this to me!

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.700
If you don't wanna come,
I'll go alone!

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.860
But the commander
ordered us to...

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.700
Don't you have
enough compassion...

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.210
...to help your boss
celebrate his good luck?

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.730
Yeah, I do! I do, but if
they find out about this...

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.580
...they're gonna do more
than just yell at us!

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.250
Fine, Michel!

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.480
When all the money comes in,
you can't be my friend!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:18.910
Huh? Money?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.710
Uh, how much money
are they paying you?

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:22.300
Who cares?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.520
Wait, please!
Take me with you!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:37.660
Are you sure it was all right
to just take this thing?

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.570
It's fine! Fine!

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:42.940
We're on an actual mission
at the moment! A recon mission!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.600
Uh, a recon mission?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.410
Yeah! Now let's really go fast!

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.350
I'll put in my request
for a discharge tomorrow!

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.680
You can be a
soldier till you die!

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.280
Don't say that!

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.790
Oh, wait! I smell women!

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.230
Hey there, ladies! I...

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.330
What's this all about?

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.890
What's going on here?!

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.740
E- Eledore...

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.410
Pressure's still low!
Do something!

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.740
We're still readjusting it.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.010
Until we find what's
damaged on it...

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.550
...do something else to stop it.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.940
What? Feddie soldiers?

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:25.680
Yes, sir.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.350
We'd better hurry
and get out of here.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:31.220
Right. Increase patrols and
hurry up on the repairs!

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:31.550
Sir!

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.190
What's the situation?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:37.890
Sir! No one's seen
either Eledore or Michel.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.230
Where did they go?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.740
<i>Yeah, th-se two w-r-</i>
<i>fly-n' pre-ty hi-h.</i>

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.740
<i>Th-y took o-f t-w-rds the</i>
<i>village in area Whiskey-208.</i>

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.440
<i>... k-nd- f-r from the Z...ks'</i>
<i>us...I st-mp...g gr...nds...</i>

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.410
<i>... so I do-bt th...'re...</i>

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.850
Lieutenant Nickard,
I can't get a clear signal!

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.510
Say again, over!

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.950
It's no use.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:06.520
All I could make out was
"village in area Whiskey-208."

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.260
That's not that
far from here.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.700
Well, it's pretty clear
they violated orders.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.930
Finding them comes first.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.780
Karen, you and I will
go out looking for them.

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.640
Right.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:20.480
Sanders, stand by here
and await communication.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:21.360
Aye, sir.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.420
You there!
Where are you going?!

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:36.120
I'm begging you!
Please let me go!

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.590
You were told no one
was allowed to leave!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.650
My baby has a fever!

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:42.790
I have to get him to the
doctor in the next village!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.860
Nobody's allowed to leave!

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:48.330
Please! If anything
happens to him!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.630
Enough!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.430
Is that really necessary?

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.910
Norris, can't we do
something about that?

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.780
This is only for while the
Apsalus is being repaired.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.680
We can't allow anyone to
leave under these circumstances.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.150
We got rooms for us here.

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.120
Miss Aina?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.130
What about the villagers?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.720
Naturally, we won't need to stay
here after the repairs are done, so...

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.230
Stop it, please!

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:21.230
Eledore!

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:23.830
Who was that?!

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.770
They must be interrogating
those Feddie soldiers.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:31.400
I can't stand this.
I'm going back to the Apsalus!

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:33.140
Miss Aina!

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.650
So? What's your unit?

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.320
Right... Th- The 408th
infantry division.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:47.590
And what did you come
to this village for?

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.130
Yeah, about that...

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.360
Eledore...

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:54.770
We wanted to see if we could
help out the glorious Zeon.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:55.890
WHAT?!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:11.610
Were you serious before?
About wanting to join the Zeon?

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:16.320
You dumbshit! If I hadn't said
that, we might already be!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:17.380
Shit!

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.760
Yeah, that's right.
You wouldn't do that, would you?

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.420
Of course not!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.060
- Um...
- What?!

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.660
Aren't you hungry?

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:29.630
We don't have time for that!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.170
They may send us to the
firing squad tomorrow!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.730
Firing squad?!

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:36.500
Surely there'd be no harm.
Just some food.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.550
They're probably going
to be executed tomorrow.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:42.740
Everyone who stays at this
hotel is treated the same.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:43.870
Miss Maria...

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:44.820
Maria?

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.180
Just don't tell my
commanders about this.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.790
Hey, Feddies!
Some food's here for you!

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.850
I'd appreciate it if you brought
some wine along next time.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.190
Maybe next time.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.500
You wait for me here.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:00.970
Oh, my. Oh, my.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:05.000
You two need medicine for
those wounds as well as food.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:10.980
Now, eat this and
try to cheer up.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.080
Here.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.690
As long as you don't lose hope,
you'll have a chance to live.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.860
So, how old are you?
Bet you're hungry, right?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.120
Please leave her alone!

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.560
Do you understand?

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:32.760
Please, Miss Maria,
I didn't mean any harm.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.200
Come, let's go.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:48.840
You still haven't given
me the key to my room.

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.880
I beg your pardon.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:56.820
It's the inner room
on the second floor.

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.120
Thanks.

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.160
Good night, Madam.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.150
Good night, sir.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.210
This is it, huh?

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:24.250
<i>This is definitely</i>
<i>area Whiskey-208.</i>

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.580
Doesn't look like anything's
wrong. Quiet village.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:32.990
What's that?

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:37.960
Heat? And steam?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.830
It's man-shaped!

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.340
A Zaku!

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.040
It's near the village.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:49.340
If Eledore and Michel
went in there...

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:54.110
Karen, I've sighted a Zaku!
Get back here!

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.810
<i>Aye, sir! Hold it!</i>
<i>Somebody's coming!</i>

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.080
Zeon?

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:01.390
<i>I don't know for sure yet.</i>
<i>Should I take him?</i>

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.680
Can you do it?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:03.820
I'll try, sir.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:17.370
Why, you!

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.470
YOU?!

00:11:33.990 --> 00:11:36.250
It's no use, Eledore.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.950
There's no way you can
get out through there.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:41.930
I'm getting out.
I'm getting out, somehow!

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:47.160
God dammit!
God dammit! God dammit!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.560
Just when I thought I was finally
gonna turn pro, this happens!

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.680
I just wanted to hear
the song they're pressing...

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:58.750
...get played once before I died!

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:00.750
Eledore...

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:05.510
I'm a musician! I'm not
cut out to be a soldier!

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.650
Even you can see that, right?!

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.590
Huh? Y- Yeah...

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.220
I wanna go home!
I don't wanna die!

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.160
Well, neither do I!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:19.500
I've been writing love songs,
dammit! "Love and Peace!"

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:23.070
And now I'm sitting in this
cellar, waiting to be shot!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.860
I finally got my big chance!

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.210
My dream's fallen apart!

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.170
Eledore!

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.880
Just leave me alone!

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.120
Miss Maria said not to
lose hope, remember?!

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:43.850
How can you be so calm
in this situation?!

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.160
My heart's broken...

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:48.990
...but I wouldn't expect YOU
to understand how I feel!

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:54.530
Don't be so self-centered!
This is all your fault, isn't it?!

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:58.500
What was that?! How dare
you say that to me!

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.540
Well, it's true!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.440
I won't even get to write a
letter to say goodbye to B.B.!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.110
I told you those long-distance love
affairs never have happy endings!

00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:11.780
Me, on the other hand...

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.480
...with the debut I've dreamed
of right in front of me!

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.550
GOD DAMN IT ALL!

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.060
Hey, that's dangerous!
Have you gone nuts?!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:23.660
Shut up! I can't
take this anymore!

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.490
Stop it, please!

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:31.730
All you've ever done is talk
about yourself, while I've!

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:33.740
I never forced you
to come with me!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.870
You see! There you go again,
not taking responsibility!

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:39.710
What?! Is that how
you talk to your senior?!

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.310
There's no senior or
junior involved here!

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.580
You always just
do what YOU want...

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:47.180
...and then expect
ME to cover your ass.

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:48.720
What?!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:52.590
I didn't do anything,
and you HIT me?!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.390
Why, you!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.660
That's playing dirty!
You big bully!

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.600
Ow! Come back here!

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.940
Now you used a weapon?!

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:13.540
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:15.480
Stop that!

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:19.780
Stop it!
Stop that right now!

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.180
Can't breathe!

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.390
Why, you! You!

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:28.490
Stop it!
Stop it, both of you!

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.760
Get away from him!

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:31.200
You don't know how
hard things are for me!

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:33.460
Why, you!
A musician's face is his life!

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:34.630
B.B.!

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.460
The repairs on the
Apsalus are complete.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.290
Good work.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.300
Miss Aina, you should
get back at once.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.840
Right. You be careful, too.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.930
What the hell?!

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.040
Is that the new Zeek weapon?!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.830
What the?!

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:53.680
A squall?
No! Shiro, look!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.450
It's that thing!

00:15:57.120 --> 00:15:59.110
It was hiding here?!

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:02.090
We don't know their troop strength!
Let's try a confusion strategy!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:02.990
<i>Roger!</i>

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.530
Halt! A Feddie attack?!
Take us back!

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:18.000
It'd be a bad joke to get
killed by a stray shot now!

00:16:18.070 --> 00:16:19.560
Eledore, look!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.840
No way. I can't do it!

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.040
What do you mean?

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:27.380
I'm no good in a mobile suit!

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.350
That's just a
construction tank!

00:16:30.390 --> 00:16:32.820
I can't do it!
I can't get into a cockpit!

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:48.960
Dammit, these things
are pissing me off!

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.270
Hurry up!
Hurry up and get on!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:52.840
I can't! Stop it!

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:55.070
You see any other way
to save ourselves?!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.900
God dammit!

00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.310
We're pulling out!
What are you doing?!

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.670
Feddies?!

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.180
Eledore! Hurry!
Hurry up and get in!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.220
No! No way!

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:09.420
Eledore!
We gotta get outta here!

00:17:09.690 --> 00:17:10.490
Is it this switch?
This one?!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.580
Shut the hatch!

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:12.820
Don't shut it!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.590
Hurry up and close it!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.290
No! Even if I see the outside,
it'll only be a monitor!

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:21.230
Dammit!

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:22.830
Let's get out of here, fast!

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.540
Take us around!

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.540
That won't work!
You've gotta shut the hatch now!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.550
Shut that hatch
and I'll KILL you!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.100
Then let me drive it!

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:37.310
If I give it to you,
you'll close the hatch!

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:48.360
Eledore, are you okay?

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:50.600
We're getting out of here!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.660
Eledore! Eledore! ELEDORE!

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:04.270
It looks like
they're retreating!

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:05.370
Hit the ones that are left!

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.040
<i>Roger!</i>

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:12.350
Eledore, let me drive!
This isn't going to work!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:13.350
You're gonna get killed!

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:17.120
Shut up! I'm going home!
I'm going home alive!

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:19.560
And I'm gonna
get my major debut!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.590
Why, you!

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:32.670
You did it! You took out
that armored car, Eledore!

00:18:32.740 --> 00:18:35.270
Home! I'm going home!

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:41.110
Eledore! Eledore,
speak to me! ELEDORE!

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:47.610
OW! My legs hurt!
My arms hurt!

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:49.660
My whole body hurts!

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:53.150
I'm a musician!
Don't cut off my arm!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.290
Shut up!

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.060
Recon mission my ass,
you selfish bastard!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.860
Michel, hold him tight!

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:01.030
Y- Yes, ma'am!

00:19:02.070 --> 00:19:05.660
H- Hold on, lady!
At least give me some anesthesia!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:06.400
SHUT UP!

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:21.450
Aye, sir.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.550
So, we'll be sending Petty
Officer Eledore to the rear line.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.130
Aye. All right, over and out.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:29.290
That kid's lucky to be alive.

00:19:30.260 --> 00:19:32.700
I never knew Karen used
to be a medical student.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:38.570
Her husband was a good surgeon
before he was killed in battle.

00:19:39.770 --> 00:19:41.400
Excuse me, Lieutenant.

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:42.970
Y- Yes?

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:45.110
We're out of disinfectant.

00:19:45.180 --> 00:19:47.110
R- Right!

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:48.940
I'll go get some right away!

00:19:49.050 --> 00:19:52.610
Oh, that's all right.
We can use this for now.

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:54.250
Oh. Uh, sure thing.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.480
Miss Maria.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.720
I'd like to thank
you for everything.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:01.390
That's all right. I should
thank you for fighting for us.

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:04.160
I'm just happy I
could be of some use.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.720
Here, you'd better get
that over to Karen. Go on.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:07.970
Right...

00:20:09.140 --> 00:20:11.130
She's quite a lady.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.400
The most wonderful
woman in the world!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:22.110
I'll just say this:
The 08th Team moves AS a team!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:26.380
If we all go off doing our own
thing, we're going to end up dead!

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:27.980
I'm sorry about this, sir!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:32.250
But I'm glad you got back okay.

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.590
Now get some sleep.

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:35.820
Y- Yes, sir...

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.430
Karen? I'm coming in.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:53.710
How is he?

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:55.180
Commander.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.680
All we need to do is
wait for his fever to drop.

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:00.190
Right. Good job today.

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.960
Asayake o mitsumeteru anata o,
Gazing at the morning glow,

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:02.750
Take care of him.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:02.820
Asayake o mitsumeteru anata o,
Gazing at the morning glow,

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:04.450
Aye, sir.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:04.630
Asayake o mitsumeteru anata o,
Gazing at the morning glow,

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.180
Don't cut it off...

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:06.590
Asayake o mitsumeteru anata o,
Gazing at the morning glow,

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:07.100
My arm... My fingers...
My major debut...

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:10.810
watashi wa miteta
I saw you there.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:11.620
My arm... My fingers...
My major debut...

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:13.180
You really want to play
music that much, you jerk?

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:16.250
Two of us...

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:16.500
futari ni, tari nai mono o kazoe tara
Two of us, finding nothing else to do, just started counting...

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:18.100
I don't want to die...

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:18.940
futari ni, tari nai mono o kazoe tara
Two of us, finding nothing else to do, just started counting...

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:21.530
You're okay now.
You're not gonna die.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:22.310
futari ni, tari nai mono o kazoe tara
Two of us, finding nothing else to do, just started counting...

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:23.660
- What's wrong?
- My arm...

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:24.310
Nandaka okashiku natte,
Finding it strangely funny,

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:26.680
See? They're still
attached. Both of them.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.450
koe o agete waratta...
we burst out laughing...

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.250
Wh- What are you doing?!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.690
Nayan da hibi no kotae nante
What is the answer for our troubling days?

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.420
A goddess...

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:38.900
Nayan da hibi no kotae nante
What is the answer for our troubling days?

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:45.130
Arukidasu koto shikanai yone
It's nothing that a little walk can't help, right?

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:45.400
You've held
up well, Eledore.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:47.230
Kasa ne au samishisa wa,
This overlapping loneliness,

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:50.200
Now, don't go hitting on the
nurses in that field hospital!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:50.270
Kasa ne au samishisa wa,
This overlapping loneliness,

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:52.240
That sounds great.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:52.330
Kasa ne au samishisa wa,
This overlapping loneliness,

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:53.040
nukumori o oshiete kureta
teach me about it warmly...

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.010
You never change, do you?

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:56.180
nukumori o oshiete kureta
teach me about it warmly...

00:21:56.180 --> 00:21:58.580
You're only alive
thanks to Karen.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.060
nukumori o oshiete kureta
teach me about it warmly...

00:21:59.260 --> 00:21:59.550
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:21:59.550 --> 00:22:01.740
You have any regards
to send to Karen?

00:22:01.740 --> 00:22:02.250
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:04.270
To that cold-blooded woman?

00:22:04.270 --> 00:22:04.350
Dakiaeba namida sae,
Let's embrace each other even in tears,

00:22:04.350 --> 00:22:05.320
Well, time to go, Commander!

00:22:05.320 --> 00:22:06.190
wake mo naku... itoshii
unconditionally... That would be lovely.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:06.980
Right

00:22:06.980 --> 00:22:08.320
wake mo naku... itoshii
unconditionally... That would be lovely.

00:22:08.320 --> 00:22:10.980
Okay, Lieutenant Nickard,
he's all yours.

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:11.060
wake mo naku... itoshii
unconditionally... That would be lovely.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:14.070
I'll take care of him!
Let's go!

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:14.500
Mirai no futari ni
The future for the both of us,

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:15.960
See you, guys.

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:16.530
Mirai no futari ni
The future for the both of us,

00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:17.230
Eledore! Get well
soon and come back!

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:20.060
Ima o wara warenai youni
In order for our smiles today not to disappear,

00:22:20.060 --> 00:22:27.030
Neh, yume o miyou yo
Hey, why don't we dream about it instead?

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:54.960
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:55.030 --> 00:22:58.650
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:02.790
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:02.870 --> 00:23:06.560
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:06.640 --> 00:23:09.730
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:10.040 --> 00:23:13.740
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:17.870
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:21.010
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:21.690 --> 00:23:24.150
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:29.020
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:34.890
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.230
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:40.670 --> 00:23:44.130
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:47.900
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:55.040
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:55.820 --> 00:23:59.150
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:03.220
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:06.960
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:13.650
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:18.260
The 08th Team
arrives at a place...

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:20.530
...where the Zeon monster
supposedly trains.

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:23.190
As we crouch there, day after day...

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:26.870
...watching our trap,
all we do is wait to ambush it.

00:24:26.940 --> 00:24:31.670
But the harsh environment
is putting us all on edge.

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:33.810
Snap out of it, guys!

00:24:33.880 --> 00:24:37.010
We need team work for
this plan to succeed!

00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:41.780
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:41.860 --> 00:24:43.850
"Battle Line on the Burning Sand."
